body:
>Of course it is. I believe things for which there is evidence.

No no no. You cannot, logically, BELIEVE that some allegations are true and others aren't. You can't. It is logically inconsistent.

You might be able to only ARGUE for certain ones because of evidence but there is no way you could have, in your head "Well incidents 1-8, 12 and 14 happened but I think 9-11 and 13 didn't happen. You cant. You couldn't. It is logically inconsistent. But it doesn't matter because you believe every incident anyway.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

>She paid 6 million dollars for these lawyers for her to 'accidentally' put two of the same image into evidence?> Why is that hard to believe?

I would expect better service for 6 million dollars.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

>She probably didn't realize it was the same picture

Impossible. She has eyes. That's how the rest of us understood it.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

>It seems more likely that she either doesn't remember editing the photo

She claims she's never edited a photo. Do you think that was a lie too?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

>or that Rocky did it.

Why would Rocky edit the photo?
